---
import PolicyPage from '../components/common/PolicyPage.astro';
---

<PolicyPage
  title="About FateTide"
  description="FateTide is a free website for yes or no tarot readings and a daily fortune with a horoscope, made for personal reflection and entertainment rather than prediction."
  path="/about/"
  heading="About FateTide"
  lead="A calm place for a yes or no card and a little guidance for today, made for reflection rather than prediction."
>
  <section aria-labelledby="what-title">
    <h2 id="what-title">What FateTide is</h2>
    <p>FateTide is a free website built around two simple things: a yes or no tarot reading, and a daily fortune that pairs your card for the day with a horoscope for your sign. It is designed to be quiet, fast, and easy to use on a phone.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/yes-or-no/">Yes or No</a>: hold a question in mind, draw one card, and get a graded answer with a reflection.</li>
      <li><a href="/today/">Today's Fortune</a>: a card for the day with short notes on love, work, money, and advice, and an optional horoscope for your sign.</li>
      <li><a href="/horoscope/">Zodiac</a>: a guide to each of the twelve signs.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="reflection-title">
    <h2 id="reflection-title">Reflection, not prediction</h2>
    <p>Tarot, astrology, and compatibility charts are old and much-loved ways of asking questions about ourselves. FateTide treats them that way. A card or a sign offers an image, a theme, and some language for thinking about a situation. It does not tell you what will happen, and nothing on this site is presented as a certain forecast.</p>
    <p>Readings are for entertainment and personal reflection. They are not medical, legal, financial, or professional advice. Please read the <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a> for the details.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="works-title">
    <h2 id="works-title">How the site works, in brief</h2>
    <p>Cards are shuffled and drawn in your own browser. Horoscopes and compatibility notes are written text that the site selects using fixed rules. Nothing is generated on the fly by an AI service or a paid API, and no account is needed. The page on <a href="/how-it-works/">how it works</a> explains each part in plain language.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
    <h2 id="privacy-title">Privacy by design</h2>
    <p>FateTide does not ask for your name, your birth details, or your questions. Your card of the day is kept only in your own browser. The <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> describes exactly what is stored and where.</p>
  </section>
</PolicyPage>
